     ppffiillccttll uunnlliinnkk ⟨--ii | --oo⟩ _h_o_o_k _h_e_a_d

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppffiillccttll utility is intended to view and change configuration of the
     pfil(9) packet filtering hooks and filters on them.

CCOOMMMMAANNDDSS
     hheeaaddss   List available packet filtering points.

     hhooookkss   List available packet filters.

     lliinnkk ⟨--ii | --oo⟩ [--aa] _h_o_o_k _h_e_a_d
             Link _h_o_o_k to _h_e_a_d.  With the --ii flag the hook will be connected
             as input and with --oo as output hook.  At least one of --ii or --oo is
             required.  By default ppffiillccttll will prepend the hook in front of
             other hooks if any present: new hook will be as close to the wire
             as possible, so that on input it will be the first filter and on
             output it will be the last.  Adding the --aa flag switches to ap‐
             pending new hook instead of prepending.

     uunnlliinnkk ⟨--ii | --oo⟩ _h_o_o_k _h_e_a_d
             Unlink _h_o_o_k on _h_e_a_d.  At least one of --ii or --oo is required.  With
             the --ii flag the hook will be removed from the input list of hooks
             and with --oo on output list.

